Subject: [PATCH 25/37] refactor: extract calculate_stop_target from
 simulate_trade
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The stop-loss/take-profit formula (entry ± ATR multiples) was only
reachable from inside simulate_trade()'s forward-looking, backtest-
only search loop. Extracted verbatim into calculate_stop_target(entry,
atr, direction) so main.py can compute the same levels for a live
order before submission — simulate_trade() itself remains backtest-
only, since determining the outcome requires the future price path,
which live trading doesn't have.

Also fixes an off-by-one that would have crept in from a naive
extraction (the original lookahead window is 19 candles, not 20 —
preserved exactly) and cleans up formatting.

16 new tests covering calculate_stop_target's BUY/SELL direction,
simulate_trade's WIN/LOSS/TIMEOUT paths, and an explicit no-look-ahead
regression test.
